---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE_CONFIG } from '../config';
---

<Layout title={`About Us & Methodology — ${SITE_CONFIG.name}`}>
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 880px; margin: 40px auto;">
    
    <div class="eyebrow">INDEPENDENT R&D STUDIO // SECRET SAUCE</div>
    <h1 style="font-size: 34px; color: var(--text-heading); margin: 12px 0 24px;">About MNEURIX // QUEST</h1>

    <div class="article-body">
      <p>
        <strong>MNEURIX // QUEST</strong> (`mneurix.quest`) is an independent, high-signal gaming news intelligence platform engineered to replace bloated legacy publications with instant, technical press breakdowns for <strong>Real-Time Strategy (RTS)</strong>, <strong>Massively Multiplayer (MMO)</strong>, <strong>Role-Playing Games (RPG)</strong>, and <strong>Gaming Hardware Silicon</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Competitive Disruption: Where Legacy Media Falls Short</h2>
      <p>
        Traditional gaming news outlets (such as IGN, GamingBolt, and PC Gamer) have become bogged down by corporate ad bloat, slow page load times (often 5+ seconds), multi-page slideshow clickbait, and generic AI filler text.
      </p>
      <p>
        MNEURIX was created to solve these exact frustrations by delivering unique gamer value:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Sub-300ms Edge Performance</strong>: Built on Astro hybrid static-site architecture deployed across DigitalOcean edge nodes, eliminating heavy tracking scripts and auto-playing video ads.</li>
        <li><strong>Zero-Slop Journalistic Directive</strong>: Multi-agent prompt protocols explicitly ban fluff words and cliché phrases (<em>"delve into"</em>, <em>"testament to"</em>, <em>"game-changer"</em>, <em>"poised to"</em>).</li>
        <li><strong>Hardware-Aware Game Coverage</strong>: Game articles don't exist in a vacuum; every breakdown includes developer press kit citations, structured minimum/recommended hardware tables, and direct links to our interactive <a href="/tools/specs-calculator">PC Specs & VRAM Calculator</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Open Community Engine</strong>: Powered by GitHub Discussions via Giscus, allowing gamers, modders, and indie devs to participate in discussions without forced account creation.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. The MNEURIX Secret Sauce: Continuous Multi-Agent Aggregation</h2>
      <p>
        At the heart of MNEURIX is an autonomous multi-agent orchestration harness that operates 24/7 with continuous self-improving triage loops:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>1. Smart Ingestion Net</strong>: Continuously polls developer press kits, official RSS feeds, and Steam News API streams.</li>
        <li><strong>2. Vector & TF-IDF Triage</strong>: Deduplicates trailer reposts and minor hotfixes, assigning an Impact Score (1-10 scale) to surface major reveals.</li>
        <li><strong>3. Fact Extraction Engine</strong>: Extracts structured JSON specifications (platforms, release windows, engine features, hardware specs) before drafting prose.</li>
        <li><strong>4. Anti-Slop Scrutiny Agent</strong>: Audits drafted text against our strict quality directives before compiling static Astro markdown artifacts.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Sector Specialization</h2>
      <p>
        We focus exclusively on high-complexity genres where mechanics, engine technology, and hardware performance matter:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>RTS Sector</strong>: Build orders, economic refineries, rollback netcode, SnowPlay engines, and competitive balance notes.</li>
        <li><strong>MMO Sector</strong>: Server mesh networking, account Warband progression, housing instances, and endgame raid lockouts.</li>
        <li><strong>RPG Sector</strong>: Skill gem socketing mechanics, dual-mastery class matrices, WASD movement integration, and procedural vs. hand-crafted world design.</li>
        <li><strong>Hardware Sector</strong>: Chinese DRAM supply expansion (CXMT DDR5), DDR5-8000+ CUDIMM/CAMM2 innovations, and 3D V-Cache CPU gaming benchmarks.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

  </div>
</Layout>
